# Mermaid Sequence Diagram

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as Rider<br/>(Browser / Chat Widget)
    participant FE as Next.js Frontend<br/>(React + Tailwind)
    participant API as API Layer<br/>(/api/routes + Express)
    participant NLU as motorcycle-nlu.service.ts<br/>Intent & Entity Extraction
    participant KB as knowledge-retrieval.service.ts<br/>MongoDB Knowledge Lookup
    participant PT as product-retrieval.service.ts<br/>RRF Product Retrieval
    participant FM as compatibility.service.ts<br/>Fitment Verdict Engine
    participant GR as grounding.service.ts<br/>Grounding Pack & Verification
    participant GEM as Gemini API<br/>(REST + Structured JSON)
    participant DB as MongoDB
    participant VH as Verification Handler

    %% ============================
    %% STEP 1: User Input
    %% ============================
    U->>FE: Send message (e.g. "Will this exhaust fit my R15 V4?")
    FE->>API: POST /api/chat {message, sessionId}

    %% ============================
    %% STEP 2: API Entry Point
    %% ============================
    API->>NLU: analyseMessage(input.message)
    NLU-->>API: NluResult {intent, motorcycle, categories, slots, confidence}

    %% ============================
    %% STEP 3: Context Loading
    %% ============================
    API->>DB: ChatConversation.findOne({sessionId})
    DB-->>API: Conversation document (messages, sessionState, garage memory)
    API->>CONVERSATION: loadContext(sessionId, userId)
    CONVERSATION-->>API: LoadedContext (garage bike, prior messages, purchasedIds, beginnerMode)

    %% ============================
    %% STEP 4: Knowledge Retrieval
    %% ============================
    API->>KB: retrieveKnowledge(nlu, odometerKm)
    KB->>DB: MaintenanceTask/SymptomRule/PartGlossary.find(...)
    DB-->>KB: KnowledgeItem[] with stable refs
    KB-->>API: KnowledgeItem[]

    %% ============================
    %% STEP 5: Product Retrieval
    %% ============================
    API->>PT: retrieveProducts(nlu, {limit, budget, extraCategories: knowledgeCategories})
    PT->>DB: Product.find(...) + ProductCompatibility.find(...) + Review.aggregate(...)
    DB-->>PT: Candidate products with review aggregates
    PT->>FM: resolveFitmentBatch(productIds, motorcycleId)
    FM->>DB: ProductCompatibility.find({product, $or:[{motorcycle}, {universal}]})
    FM->>DB: Product.find({partCategory}) for NO_FIT inference
    DB-->>FM: Fitment links + product catalog
    FM-->>PT: Map<productId, FitmentResult {verdict, explanation}>
    PT-->>API: RetrievedProduct[] (with fitment verdicts, retrievalScore, channels)

    %% ============================
    %% STEP 6: Grounding Pack Construction
    %% ============================
    API->>GR: buildGroundingPack(message, nlu, products, reasonsByProduct, knowledge, escalate, odometerKm)
    GR->>API: GroundingPack object

    %% ============================
    %% STEP 7: Gemini Generation (conditional)
    %% ============================
    GR->>GEM: generateStructured<GroundedAnswer>({systemInstruction, history, prompt, responseSchema})
    
    alt GEMINI_CONFIGURED
        GEM->>GEM: Google Generative Language API REST call
        GEM-->>GEM: JSON response (answer + citedProductIds + citedKnowledgeRefs)
    else NOT_CONFIGURED
        GEM-->>GR: GeminiNotConfiguredError
    end

    %% ============================
    %% STEP 8: Verification
    %% ============================
    GR->>VH: verifyAnswer(candidate, pack)
    VH->>GR: VerificationResult {ok, failures, answer}
    
    alt VERIFICATION_PASSED
        VH->>GR: {ok: true, answer: finalAnswer}
        GR-->>API: Grounded answer ready for persistence
    else VERIFICATION_FAILED_ATTEMPT_1
        VH->>GR: {ok: false, failures: [violation1, ...], answer: partial}
        GR->>GR: buildRepairPrompt(failures)
        GR->>GEM: generateStructured<GroundedAnswer>({... repair prompt ...})
        GEM->>GEM: Second attempt (temperature 0.2)
        GEM-->>GEM: JSON response (may still fail)
        GEM-->>GR: Second attempt result
        GR->>VH: verifyAnswer(secondAttempt, pack)
        VH->>GR: VerificationResult {ok, failures, answer}
        
        alt VERIFICATION_PASSED_ON_RETRY
            VH->>GR: {ok: true, answer: finalAnswer}
        else VERIFICATION_FAILED_AFTER_2_ATTEMPTS
            VH->>GR: {ok: false, failures: all, answer: ''}
            GR->>API: Trigger deterministic fallback
        end
    end

    %% ============================
    %% STEP 9: Deterministic Fallback (if needed)
    %% ============================
    alt FALLBACK_PATH
        GR->>EXPLANATION: deterministicReply(nlu, products, knowledge, reasonsByProduct, escalate)
        EXPLANATION-->>GR: Complete reply string + reason summaries
        GR-->>API: Final reply (no LLM involvement)
    end

    %% ============================
    %% STEP 10: Persistence & Analytics
    %% ============================
    API->>CONVERSATION: persistTurn({sessionId, turnId, nlu, reply, products, knowledge, aiGenerated, answerTier, verificationFailures, ...})
    CONVERSATION->>DB: ChatConversation.updateOne(...) (append messages, advance state)
    DB-->>CONVERSATION: Updated conversation document
    
    API->>ANALYTICS: ChatAnalyticsEvent.create({sessionId, turnId, intent, motorcycle, categories, recommendedProducts, knowledgeRefs, aiGenerated, answerTier, verificationFailures, latencyMs})
    DB-->>ANALYTICS: Analytics event written
    
    alt VERIFICATION_FAILURES_RECORDED
        GR->>VIOLATIONS: recordViolations({sessionId, turnId, failures, pack, model, attempt, resolvedBy})
        DB-->>VIOLATIONS: GroundingViolation document written
    end

    %% ============================
    %% STEP 11: Response to User
    %% ============================
    API->>FE: JSON {reply, turnId, products: ChatProductCard[], knowledge: ChatKnowledgeCard[], meta}
    FE->>U: Render chat response with:
    - Assistant message text
    - Fitment verdict chips (FITS/NO_FIT/UNKNOWN)
    - Reason chips (CONFIRMED_FITMENT, CATEGORY_EXACT, HIGHLY_RATED, etc.)
    - Knowledge source citations
    - Product cards with pricing and fitment labels
    - Feedback buttons (thumbs up/down)
    
    %% Feedback loop (optional)
    U->>FE: Thumbs up/down on turn
    FE->>API: POST /api/chat/feedback {turnId, rating}
    API->>FE: Confirmation
    API->>DB: ChatFeedback.updateOne({turnId}, {$set: {rating, ...}})
```

### Diagram Notes:

1. **All database queries go through Mongoose** — the sequence shows conceptual DB calls; actual implementation uses Mongoose query methods with the indexes described in the database architecture section.

2. **Gemini is conditional** — if `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `GEMINI_MODEL` are not set in the environment, the system throws `GeminiNotConfiguredError` at Step 7 and immediately falls back to the deterministic reply path.

3. **Single retry only** — the verification loop allows exactly one retry (attempt 1 → repair prompt → attempt 2). A second failure triggers the deterministic fallback.

4. **Verification failures are measured** — every failure path records to `GroundingViolation`, enabling the thesis metric: `hallucination_rate = |GroundingViolations| / |ChatAnalyticsEvents|`.

5. **Knowledge refs are stable citations** — every `KnowledgeItem` carries a `ref` like `"SymptomRule:overheating"` or `"MaintenanceTask:engine-oil-change"`; every `RetrievedProduct` carries a `fitmentEvidenceId` linking to the `ProductCompatibility._id`. These are the citations verified by `verifyAnswer()`.
```